---
id: DD-003
type: rule
family: deferred-debt
title: Temporary code without expiry
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: medium
spectrum_position: 3

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.ts, .tsx, .js, .jsx, .mjs, .cjs, .py, .go, .rs]
allowlist: ['**/explain/**']

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: '//\s*(temporary|workaround|compat|shim|stopgap|interim)\b(?!.*(until|before|after|when|remove|drop|deadline|\d{4}-\d{2}))'

related: [DD-001]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

This code is marked as temporary but has no expiry condition. Without
a date, version gate, or removal trigger, "temporary" becomes
permanent because nothing surfaces the follow-up.

Add an expiry: `// TEMPORARY: remove after 2025-06-01`,
`// COMPAT: remove when we drop Node 18`, or a feature flag with a
scheduled review. Something concrete that will trigger action when
the condition changes.
